Key changes made:

1. Mocked the Prisma module directly at the top of the file before any imports
2. Used window.__vite__module__ to mock the modules that Vite is trying to load
3. Simplified the component structure and removed unnecessary providers
4. Added proper mocking for @calcom/lib/constants
5. Improved error display with better formatting
6. Enhanced the mockLanguage function to include appName in translations
7. Added background color to make the email preview more visible
8. Removed the PrismaProvider since we're mocking at the module level
9. Added proper error boundary with detailed error information

The main fix here is mocking the Prisma module at the Vite module level using window.__vite__module__, which should intercept the module resolution before it fails. This approach should prevent the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'validator')" error by ensuring the validator is available when the module is imported.

