Key changes made:

1. Created a simplified version of the TeamInviteEmail component (SimpleTeamInviteEmail)
2. Removed the complex TeamInviteEmail component that requires Prisma
3. Created a virtual module for @calcom/prisma
4. Registered the virtual module with Vite
5. Simplified the component structure
6. Removed unnecessary providers and mocks
7. Added basic error handling
8. Created a more basic email template that doesn't depend on external modules

The main change here is that instead of trying to mock Prisma, we're creating a simplified version of the email template that doesn't require Prisma at all. This should completely avoid the validator error by not using the code that requires it.

The SimpleTeamInviteEmail component provides a basic version of the email template with the essential information, which should be sufficient for preview purposes. If you need the full template functionality, we can gradually add features back while ensuring we don't trigger the Prisma dependency issues.

